WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.526
Welcome to Grade 8 English, Unit
7: Historical Figures and Legacy.

2
00:00:04.606 --> 00:00:05.433
In this unit,

3
00:00:05.513 --> 00:00:13.599
you will explore the theme of Historical Figures and Legacy
- a topic that invites you to think about how individuals

4
00:00:13.679 --> 00:00:17.856
shape history and how their actions echo through generations.

5
00:00:17.936 --> 00:00:23.858
The centrepiece is an original story, "The
Rebellion of Silence", which follows Jamal,

6
00:00:23.938 --> 00:00:29.022
a quiet but determined student at an
East African boarding school in 1948,

7
00:00:29.102 --> 00:00:33.070
as his anonymous essays challenge an unjust ban on debate.

8
00:00:33.150 --> 00:00:40.398
Alongside the story, you will master the grammar of
narrating the past - Past Simple and Past Continuous,

9
00:00:40.478 --> 00:00:46.958
the Past Perfect, reported speech, verbs with
prepositions, phrasal verbs, reflexive pronouns,

10
00:00:47.038 --> 00:00:54.007
time phrases and discourse markers - and build a
rich vocabulary for discussing argument, leadership,

11
00:00:54.087 --> 00:00:55.333
emotion and change.

12
00:00:55.413 --> 00:01:01.195
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

13
00:01:01.275 --> 00:01:03.056
By the end of this unit,

14
00:01:03.136 --> 00:01:12.205
you will be able to use the Past Simple and Past Continuous
tenses correctly to narrate events and describe actions in

15
00:01:12.285 --> 00:01:13.833
progress in the past.

16
00:01:13.913 --> 00:01:22.129
You will also form and use the Past Perfect tense to
show which action happened first when telling a story.

17
00:01:22.209 --> 00:01:31.122
You will also convert direct speech into Reported Speech,
adjusting pronouns, verb tenses, and word order correctly.

18
00:01:31.202 --> 00:01:33.991
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

19
00:01:34.071 --> 00:01:40.649
Your vocabulary work begins with these words: benign,
reprieve, defect, disposition, systematic, cache.

20
00:01:40.729 --> 00:01:45.885
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

21
00:01:45.965 --> 00:01:49.957
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

22
00:01:50.037 --> 00:01:55.892
The reading sequence includes Legacy: The People
History Remembers and The Storyteller's Toolkit:

23
00:01:55.972 --> 00:01:57.299
Talking About the Past.

24
00:01:57.379 --> 00:01:58.156
Read actively.

25
00:01:58.236 --> 00:02:02.378
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

26
00:02:02.458 --> 00:02:06.355
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

27
00:02:06.435 --> 00:02:10.473
The first language focus is Past Simple vs Past Continuous.

28
00:02:10.553 --> 00:02:18.082
The Past Simple reports a finished action, while the
Past Continuous shows an action in progress across time;

29
00:02:18.162 --> 00:02:22.479
used together, they let one event
interrupt another in a story.

30
00:02:22.559 --> 00:02:30.088
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

31
00:02:30.168 --> 00:02:35.219
In speaking, you will complete Speaking
1: The Rebellion of Silence Retold.

32
00:02:35.299 --> 00:02:39.802
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

33
00:02:39.882 --> 00:02:43.291
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

34
00:02:43.371 --> 00:02:46.917
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

35
00:02:46.997 --> 00:02:48.613
You are ready to begin.

36
00:02:48.693 --> 00:02:55.910
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

37
00:02:55.990 --> 00:02:59.448
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

38
00:02:59.528 --> 00:03:07.630
Use AI English for hints and feedback any time, and bring
your questions to a live session too if you join one.
